            <ArticleTitle>Nose-bronchi link: does an asthma march exist?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>941-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Allergic rhinitis is considered a strong risk factor for the onset of asthma. However, few studies have addressed this issue from a functional point of view. In this work the close link between upper and lower airways is highlighted, suggesting that spirometry should be precociously performed on patients with allergic rhinitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
